                                                "sense_id": "63270732-4a28-3941-8b1e-4f4c2dd29ab7",
                                                "text": "i only disclose my pronouns when i'm absolutely sure no one will spew exorsexist, \"they is only for multiple people\", garbage at me"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "975c7cb2-7d8e-460a-b198-56e266afb4e0",
                                                "sense_id": "63270732-4a28-3941-8b1e-4f4c2dd29ab7",
                                                "text": "got my first exorsexist \"its a guy\" comment about a nonbinary character! im finally moving up in the world!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7074e94-daf6-450d-8e39-0eab4632f741",
                                                "sense_id": "63270732-4a28-3941-8b1e-4f4c2dd29ab7",
                                                "text": "However, there can be added tension due to rules of conduct that exist in medical settings that could make the atmosphere palpably uncomfortable. In such situations, there are obligations of the individual being treated as to how they need to behave (i.e., that they must not get mad or otherwise “lose control” if the doctor is being exorsexist) and expectations of how the doctor or nurse (practitioner) should treat them which may not be met in the appointment"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c59de252-faf6-403a-8ae0-0af01065436c",
                                                "sense_id": "63270732-4a28-3941-8b1e-4f4c2dd29ab7",
                                                "text": "This squares with the ways in which obscuring how transmasculine people are specifically targeted is incentivized in our society [64] and how LLM’s can struggle to recognize the transmisogyny often implied by anti-transmasculine or exorsexist content, or the transmisogyny inherent to racist degendering of cis women of color [38, 53, 64]"
                                            }
                                        ]
